        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(workspace): make bootstrap file read retry backoff abortable",
        "body": "## Summary\nWire an optional `AbortSignal` through the workspace bootstrap call chain so retry backoff in `readWorkspaceFileWithGuards` and `fileContentDiffersFromTemplate` is interruptible by caller cancellation.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nThe workspace bootstrap file reader (`readWorkspaceFileWithGuards`) uses `retryAsync` to handle transient filesystem races (EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK/EINTR). The retry backoff between attempts uses the default `setTimeout`-based sleep, which is not interruptible. When the caller has an abort context (e.g., agent turn cancellation), the backoff delay blocks until completion.\n\n**Code evidence**: In `src/agents/workspace.ts:93` and `:284`, both `retryAsync` calls lacked an abortable `sleep` option. The exported functions (`loadWorkspaceBootstrapFiles`, `loadExtraBootstrapFilesWithDiagnostics`, `resolveBootstrapFilesForRun`, `resolveBootstrapContextForRun`) had no signal parameter to thread down.\n\n## Root Cause\n`retryAsync` defaults to `setTimeout(resolve, ms)` for its backoff sleep. Without a custom `sleep` function that uses `sleepWithAbort(ms, signal)`, the retry backoff is not abortable. The call chain from top-level bootstrap resolution down to the retry helpers had no signal parameter, so even callers with access to an abort signal couldn't pass it through.\n\n## Why This Fix\nAdd an optional `signal?: AbortSignal` parameter at each level of the call chain:\n- `resolveBootstrapContextForRun` → `resolveBootstrapFilesForRun` → `getOrLoadBootstrapFiles` → `loadWorkspaceBootstrapFiles` → `readWorkspaceFileWithGuards`\n- `loadExtraBootstrapFilesWithDiagnostics` → `readWorkspaceFileWithGuards`\n- `fileContentDiffersFromTemplate` (internal)\n\nWhen provided, the retry backoff uses `sleepWithAbort(ms, signal)` so cancellation interrupts the delay immediately. When omitted (default), behavior is unchanged. The signal is always optional and backward-compatible.\n\nFollows the identical pattern as:\n- PR #109805: `fix(auto-reply): honor abortSignal in transient-HTTP retry backoff`\n- PR #109913: `fix(discord): honor caller abortSignal during 429 retry backoff`\n- PR #110427: `fix(compaction): make retry backoff abortable with caller signal`\n\n## User Impact\n- **Before**: Cancelling during workspace bootstrap file reads with transient errors would wait for the full backoff delay. The bare `setTimeout` cannot be interrupted.\n- **After**: When callers thread an abort signal through the chain, cancellation interrupts the retry backoff immediately. No behavior change for existing callers (signal defaults to undefined).\n\n## Evidence\n- Wall-clock proof demonstrates the mechanism: `retryAsync` without `sleepWithAbort` takes 1502ms to notice an abort fired at 50ms; with `sleepWithAbort`, it notices in ~51ms.\n- The signal is threaded end-to-end from the public API (`resolveBootstrapContextForRun`) through `bootstrap-files.ts` → `bootstrap-cache.ts` → `workspace.ts` to the internal retry helpers.\n- `sleepWithAbort` is well-tested in `@openclaw/retry` and used by 10+ call sites across the codebase.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Before (bare setTimeout, no signal)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-workspace-retry-abort.mjs\n=== BEFORE (bare setTimeout, no signal) ===\n{\n  \"elapsedMs\": 1502,\n  \"calls\": 2,\n  \"verdict\": \"FAIL: abort did not interrupt backoff\"\n}\n```\nAbort fired at ~50ms; the retry still waited the full 1500ms backoff and attempted a 2nd call.\n\n### After (sleepWithAbort)\n```bash\n=== AFTER (sleepWithAbort) ===\n{\n  \"elapsedMs\": 51,\n  \"calls\": 1,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS: abort interrupted backoff immediately\"\n}\n```\nSame abort timing; the backoff was interrupted in ~1ms and no retry was attempted.\n\n## Tests and Validation\n- `pnpm check` passed\n- New regression test in `src/agents/workspace.test.ts`: \"aborts promptly during retry backoff when the caller signal fires\" — verifies abort interrupts the retry delay with fake timers and confirms timer cleanup\n- Existing workspace tests unchanged — the optional signal parameter is backward-compatible\n",
